1	//! Alias / pointer-provenance categorization for memory accesses.
2	//!
3	//! Each `LOAD` / `STORE` instruction can carry an optional
4	//! [`AliasCategory`] tag describing what kind of memory it touches.
5	//! Downstream optimization passes consult the tag to decide whether the
6	//! access is safe to fold, propagate through, or eliminate:
7	//!
8	//! * `Stack`, `Heap`, `Static`, `Unknown` — passes apply their current
9	//!   conservative behavior unchanged.
10	//! * `Mmio` and `Volatile` — passes must treat the access as opaque:
11	//!   never propagate a constant past it, never eliminate it even if it
12	//!   appears dead.
13	//!
14	//! The metadata is **additive**: existing IR shape, golden text dumps,
15	//! and printer output are unaffected. `None` (the default) preserves
16	//! pre-existing pass behavior.
17	//!
18	//! Categorization is performed at lift time (or shortly after, in
19	//! `unlace_passes::alias_categorize`) using:
20	//!
21	//! | Category | Heuristic                                                              |
22	//! |----------|------------------------------------------------------------------------|
23	//! | `Stack`  | base is RSP/RBP / arch-stack-register                                  |
24	//! | `Static` | constant address falls inside a known `.data`/`.bss`/`.rodata` section |
25	//! | `Heap`   | base flows from a recognised allocator call (malloc/calloc/realloc …) |
26	//! | `Mmio`   | constant address in a known MMIO range (per-arch, off by default)      |
27	//! | `Volatile` | explicit DWARF/PDB `volatile` qualifier                              |
28	//! | `Unknown`  | everything else                                                      |
